From: Senemos Uke contributors
Subject: [PATCH] clk: qcom: size the Cliffs probe snapshot from its actual table

The v7.2 port preserves upstream RPMh clock IDs and assigns CXO_PAD IDs 29/30.
The inherited 29-entry restore snapshot therefore rejected the 31-entry Cliffs
provider before any clock could register. Derive all snapshot bounds from the
provider itself. Keep the probe guard and failure restoration behavior.
Stock DT consumers of downstream IDs 27/28 must be translated to 29/30 in the
first-console adaptation; do not redefine upstream LN_BB_CLK4 IDs globally.

Source: existing attributed clk-rpmh-uke.c port and upstream qcom,rpmh.h
License: GPL-2.0-only

--- a/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rpmh-uke.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-rpmh-uke.c
@@ -433,9 +433,9 @@
 
 struct clk_rpmh_uke_snapshot {
 	const struct clk_rpmh_desc *desc;
-	struct clk_hw *clks[29];
-	const struct clk_init_data *init[29];
-	u32 addr[29];
+	struct clk_hw *clks[ARRAY_SIZE(cliffs_rpmh_clocks)];
+	const struct clk_init_data *init[ARRAY_SIZE(cliffs_rpmh_clocks)];
+	u32 addr[ARRAY_SIZE(cliffs_rpmh_clocks)];
 };
 
 static void clk_rpmh_uke_restore(void *data)
